{
  "summary": "Bundled `cookie-universal` library (a self-contained webpack bundle with its own module runtime) that also embeds the `cookie` package (`parse`/`serialize`). The exported factory `(req, res, parseJSON = true)` detects client vs server context and returns an API `{ parseJSON, set, setAll, get, getAll, remove, removeAll, nodeCookie }` that reads cookies from `document.cookie` or the request `cookie` header / response `Set-Cookie` headers, writes via `document.cookie` or `res.setHeader('Set-Cookie', ...)`, JSON-stringifies object values and optionally JSON-parses values on read; removal sets `expires` to epoch. The embedded serializer validates names/values and supports Max-Age, Domain, Path, Expires, HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite.",
  "exports": {
    "module.exports": "cookie-universal factory (req, res, parseJSON) returning the cookie API object"
  },
